         text="The Yongle emperor, who had seized the throne from Nanjing in 1402 and had ruled the north as Prince of Yan, held the New Year audience in his new palace and proclaimed Beijing the chief capital. Envoys from Timurid Herat, who were present, described the vast halls, the crowds of officials and the elephants at the gates.",
